,title,link,text,language,family
0,Music of Ukraine - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Ukraine,2 weeks ago - The music of Ukraine covers diverse and multiple component elements of Western and Eastern European music. It has indigenous Slavic and Christian elements. The Ukrainian lands were the musical heartland of the former Russian Empire.,Ukrainian,Indo-European
1,Ukrainian folk music - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ukrainian_folk_music,"September 3, 2025 - Ukrainian folk music includes a number of varieties of traditional, folkloric, folk-inspired popular music, and folk-inspired European classical music traditions. In the 20th century numerous ethnographic and folkloric musical ensembles were established in Ukraine and gained popularity. During the Soviet era, music was a controlled commodity and was used as a tool for the indoctrination ...",Ukrainian,Indo-European
2,Category:Ukrainian styles of music - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Ukrainian_styles_of_music,"Ukrainian jazz (2 C) The following 2 pages are in this category, out of 2 total. This list may not reflect recent changes. Choral concerto · Dumka (musical genre) Categories: Music of Ukraine · European music genres · Search · Category:Ukrainian styles of music ·",Ukrainian,Indo-European
3,"Ukrainian Music | Center for Russian, East European, & Eurasian Studies",https://crees.ku.edu/ukrainian-music,"The selection combines carefully picked and beautiful songs along with Ukrainian English-translated lyrics. ... Maria Sonevytsky, an Associate Professor of Anthropology and Music at Michigan State University, reflects on how the war in Ukraine is echoed in its music as a form of cultural expression.",Ukrainian,Indo-European
4,Chapter 11: Music: A Map of Ukrainian History – Being Ukraine,https://openpress.digital.conncoll.edu/beingukraine/chapter/chapter-9/,"December 10, 2022 - However, the lasting legacy of the Lydian people is most evident in what is known as the Lydian mode. The musical themes of the Lydian Mode were viewed as effeminate in Greek society, however, the Lydian Mode can be seen in much of traditional Ukrainian music.",Ukrainian,Indo-European
5,Ukrainian Folk Music,https://geofolk.ge/en/article/ukrainuli-khalkhuri-musika/60,The relatively late Ukrainian oral-and-written folk music culture is lyrical in nature. It acquired its distinct style in the eighteenth century and originated in upper-class circles. The influence of European (Polish) intonations is obvious.,Ukrainian,Indo-European
6,"Modern Ukrainian Music | Center for Russian, East European, & Eurasian Studies",https://crees.ku.edu/modern-ukrainian-music,"She states in her LinkedIn bio: ""my main goal is to make Ukrainian music new worldwide music trend.” ... Jerry Hail’s fame rose after the release of #ОХРАНА_ОТМЄНА (#SECURITY_CANCELLATION) which she posted on Instagram. The song went viral and led to her popularity.",Ukrainian,Indo-European
7,FolkWorld #48: Music of Ukraine,http://www.folkworld.de/48/e/ukraine.html,"Traditional instrumental ensembles are often known as troïstï muzyki (literally ‘three musicians’ that typically make up the ensemble, e.g. violin, sopilka and buben). When performing dance melodies instrumental performance usually includes improvisation. The traditional dances of Ukraine include: the Kozak, Kozachok, Tropak, Hopak, Hrechanyky, Kolomyjka and Hutsulka, Metelytsia, Shumka, Arkan, Kateryna (Kadryl) and Chabarashka. Dances originating outside the Ukrainian ethnic region but which are also popular include: the Polka, Mazurka, Krakowiak, Csárdás, Waltz, Kamarynska and Barynya.",Ukrainian,Indo-European
8,Ukrainian Folk Music - ku crees - The University of Kansas,https://crees.ku.edu/ukrainian-folk-music,"Folk music is a genre of traditional songs passed down through generations with commonalities such as origin, language, culture, history, religion, traditions, or customs. Folk songs often lack a single author and feature traditional instruments. The lyrics and melodies tend to have regional · Traditional instruments featured in Ukrainian folk music include the trembita, sopilka, bandura, tsymbaly, domra, and kobza.",Ukrainian,Indo-European
9,10 Reasons Why Ukrainian Music is a World-Class Phenomenon - UkraineWorld,https://ukraineworld.org/en/articles/ukraine-explained/10-reasons-why-ukrainian-music-world-class-phenomenon,"According to the Yuri Chekan, Lecturer at the Tchaikovsky National Academy of Music, professional performers were already at work by the end of the tenth century. Back in the time of the Kyiv Rus, they emerged with the introduction of the Christian Church, extending the Gregorian chant tradition and singing the oldest hymns of Byzantium and Rome. But Ukrainian choral art transformed significantly over the years into the Old Kyivan znamennyi chant, passing directly from medieval to Baroque style, unlike West European culture.",Ukrainian,Indo-European
